fix(ci): Improve Coolify deployment error handling and polling
scale: ~24 lines across 1 files [S]

- `.github/workflows/deploy-hetzner.yml`:
    - Modified the handling of HTTP 403 errors during Coolify deployment status polling:
        - Changed the error message from `::error::` to `::warning::` when the `COOLIFY_TOKEN` lacks read permissions.
        - The workflow now skips polling and exits with `0` (success) instead of `1` (failure) in this scenario, relying on the public `/health` probe for verification.
        - Added a new output `deploy_status=skipped_poll_no_read` to indicate this behavior.
    - Modified the handling of Coolify application API health checks (`GET /api/v1/applications/{uuid}`):
        - Added a specific warning for HTTP 403 errors, indicating that the token lacks read permissions and that the public `/health` probe will be authoritative.
        - Added a success message for HTTP 200 responses.
        - The check now only exits with an error for non-200/403 HTTP statuses.

